# game.pdl - what the editor's PLAY does for this book. Made by game_new_op (template _common/game.pdl); the shared core's `play` verb reads it (petslike_core.c book_driver()).
# GAME | driver | <program> <args...>   run on Play (detached, one instance: the program locks itself). {house} {book} {editor} are replaced by the house root, this book's folder and the editor's folder.
# The driver is the game's loop: it ticks only while the editor's switch running=1 (Player > Play / Stop), and publishes the game bar feed state/game_ui.txt that the editor window draws. It decides no game rule:
# every rule is in the shared engine (game_core, data in rulesets/default/) and the ledger is the only authority.
# GAME | kind   ledger | realtime | editor   (the first ledger row records it; a replay refuses a ledger of another kind)
# GAME | clock  pause | run   pause = the editor's world clock is paused while this game is live (feed gm_on=1) and resumes by itself when it ends.
GAME   | name        | teario-play
GAME   | title       | Teario-Play
GAME   | kind        | realtime
GAME   | ruleset     | default
GAME   | driver      | {house}/&.widgits/_shared-lib/ops/+x/game_core.+x driver {house} {book} {editor}
GAME   | clock       | pause
# GAME | export  (data-hq P0): the data studio's exporter row (game.csv, events.csv, schema.pdl). The editor's Play ignores it.
GAME   | export      | {house}/&.widgits/_shared-lib/ops/+x/game_core.+x {book} {state} export {out}
GAME   | ui_mode     | play
GAME   | own_run     | 1
# D104: a run folder may hold level.pdl (written by Teario-Make's `play` verb: the level being edited); it is read INSTEAD of the LEVEL file of board.pdl and its text is part of the rules hash, so a run of another level is refused
GAME   | level_in_run | 1
